A||||8||rogergarrison||Another Store Self Check Out Story||||1||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||12-31-2001||06:46 AM||||Well I just needed a can of spray paint. Stand in a line to give these things one more chance since the ones with clerks had over 25 people each. Finally get to the machine and after running it by scanner a few times, finally beeps that its recognized it.....wow. Ok, so maybe it does work. Now the screen flashes me to show my ID. WTF? Im not going to get my Drivers licence out of my wallet and show it to pay cash for a $3 can of paint. Left it on the scanner and walked out the door. From now on when I go in any store, Im looking to see if the clerks line is full before I even go to find anything. If they are, Im out the door.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||12-31-2001||08:34 AM||||Uh, who exactly where you supposed to show id to?<P>BTW, the reason it <B>probably</B> asked for your id is because in most states it is illegal to sell spraypaint, fat markers, ets. to minors. You know, to keep the graffitti off the side of your business. How's that working?<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-31-2001||09:17 AM||||no gaffitti here. If they did, id have em on video tape anyway, and in front of it would be a big blood stain, hehe.<P>I guess i was supposed to run it thru card scanner or something which any kid could also do with someone elses ID. So kinda useless idea unless its a photo ID and looks thru a camera to compare your face to. And Im not about to do it for a $3 purchase. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||12-31-2001||09:24 AM||||Well, here, you have to show your ID to a customer service rep.  So much for the self-service checkout saving man-power.  The last time I used one they had the manager and another employee there to help people operate the self-service checkout.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  The same 2 people could have checked everyone out in half the time.  Dumbest thing I've ever seen.  ||||reg||1
